-- coa11-part16-ch2-public.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 16 (Audit), Chapter 2 (Appointment of auditors),
-- the cross-heading "Public companies": ss 489 to 491 (with 489A, 489B, 489C, 490A and 491A): raw lines 6797-6879.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no seat, no point of view.  Reading a result, the polarity of names and inputs: as in
-- coa11-part16-ch1.l4.  The public company provisions mirror ss 485 to 488 with "accounts meeting" for "period for
-- appointing auditors"; there is no counterpart of s 488 (a public company has no deemed re-appointment).
-- Every top-level name, type, constructor and field begins with the label of the provision it implements.

§ `Part 16 Chapter 2: Appointment of auditors: public companies (ss 489 to 491)`

§§ `s 489 Appointment of auditors of public company: general`

-- src:6799 | (1) An auditor or auditors of a public company must be appointed for each financial year of the company, unless the directors reasonably resolve otherwise on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required.
@ref s 489(1) An auditor must be appointed for each financial year (src:6799-6799)
GIVEN `the company is a public company (section 4(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have resolved that no auditor be appointed for the financial year on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors' resolution was a reasonable one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 489(1) an auditor or auditors of the public company must be appointed for the financial year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the company is a public company (section 4(2))`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An auditor or auditors of a public company"
        IF `the directors have resolved that no auditor be appointed for the financial year on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required` AND `the directors' resolution was a reasonable one`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the directors reasonably resolve otherwise on the ground that audited accounts are unlikely to be required" (the unless is met: fork F3)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:6800 | (2) For each financial year for which an auditor or auditors is or are to be appointed (other than the company's first financial year), the appointment must be made before the end of the accounts meeting of the company at which the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are laid.
@ref s 489(2) The appointment must be made before the end of the accounts meeting (src:6800-6800)
GIVEN `the appointment is for the company's first financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 437 the day the accounts meeting at which the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are laid ends` IS A DATE
      `the day the appointment is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 489(2) the appointment is made before the end of the accounts meeting` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appointment is for the company's first financial year`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(other than the company's first financial year)"
        IF `the day the appointment is made` AT MOST `s 437 the day the accounts meeting at which the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are laid ends`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- an appointment on the day the meeting ends counts as before its end: the time of day is not modelled (fork F6)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the appointment must be made before the end of the accounts meeting of the company at which the company's annual accounts and reports for the previous financial year are laid" (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:6801 | (3) The directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company—
-- src:6802 | (a) at any time before the company's first accounts meeting;
-- src:6803 | (b) following a period during which the company (being exempt from audit) did not have any auditor, at any time before the company's next accounts meeting;
-- src:6804 | (c) to fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor.
@ref s 489(3) The directors may appoint an auditor (src:6801-6804)
GIVEN `the appointment is made at any time before the company's first accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made following a period during which the company, being exempt from audit, did not have any auditor, at a time before the company's next accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made to fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 489(3) the directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company` MEANS
    IF    `the appointment is made at any time before the company's first accounts meeting`
       OR `the appointment is made following a period during which the company, being exempt from audit, did not have any auditor, at a time before the company's next accounts meeting`
       OR `the appointment is made to fill a casual vacancy in the office of auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company— (a) at any time before ..., (b) following a period ..., (c) to fill a casual vacancy": a grant that names its occasions (fork F13)

-- src:6805 | (4) The members may appoint an auditor or auditors by ordinary resolution—
-- src:6806 | (a) at an accounts meeting;
-- src:6807 | (b) if the company should have appointed an auditor or auditors at an accounts meeting but failed to do so;
-- src:6808 | (c) where the directors had power to appoint under subsection (3) but have failed to make an appointment.
@ref s 489(4) The members may appoint by ordinary resolution (src:6805-6808)
GIVEN `the appointment is made at an accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company should have appointed an auditor or auditors at an accounts meeting but failed to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors had power to appoint under subsection (3) but have failed to make an appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 489(4) the members may appoint an auditor or auditors of the company by ordinary resolution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   `the appointment is made at an accounts meeting`
                OR `the company should have appointed an auditor or auditors at an accounts meeting but failed to do so`
                OR `the directors had power to appoint under subsection (3) but have failed to make an appointment`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members may appoint an auditor or auditors by ordinary resolution— (a) at an accounts meeting; (b) if ...; (c) where ..."
        IF `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 282 the resolution is an ordinary resolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by ordinary resolution": the grant is of an appointment by that kind of resolution
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 282 is not known

-- src:6809 | (5) An auditor or auditors of a public company may only be appointed—
-- src:6810 | (a) in accordance with this section, or
-- src:6811 | (b) in accordance with section 490 or 490A (default power of Secretary of State).
@ref s 489(5) Only in accordance with this section, section 490 or section 490A (src:6809-6811)
GIVEN `the appointment is made in accordance with section 489` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is made in accordance with section 490 or 490A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 489(5) the appointment is made in accordance with a route the section allows` MEANS
    IF `the appointment is made in accordance with section 489` OR `the appointment is made in accordance with section 490 or 490A`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- "may only be appointed— (a) in accordance with this section, or (b) in accordance with section 490 or 490A": JUST TRUE says only that this subsection does not bar it
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An auditor or auditors of a public company may only be appointed— (a) in accordance with this section, or (b) in accordance with section 490 or 490A"

§§ `s 489A Appointment of auditors of public company: additional requirements for public interest entities with audit committees`

-- The text shows omitted words as "..." in s 489A(3)(b) and (4) (finding 2); the encoding follows the words as shown.

-- src:6813 | (1) This section applies to the appointment under section 489(4) of an auditor or auditors of a public company—
-- src:6814 | (a) which is also a public interest entity; and
-- src:6815 | (b) which has an audit committee.
-- src:6816 | (2) But it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company.
@ref s 489A(1) and (2) Where the section applies (src:6813-6816)
GIVEN `the appointment is made under section 489(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company (section 4(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 494A the company has an audit committee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company (section 494A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 489A(1) the section applies to the appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appointment is of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company (section 494A)`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But it does not apply to the appointment of an Auditor General as auditor or one of the auditors of the company"
        IF    `the appointment is made under section 489(4)` AND `the company is a public company (section 4(2))`
          AND `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `s 494A the company has an audit committee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 494A the company is a public interest entity` EQUALS NOTHING OR `s 494A the company has an audit committee` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a public interest entity, or has an audit committee, is not known
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to the appointment under section 489(4) of an auditor or auditors of a public company— (a) which is also a public interest entity; and (b) which has an audit committee": a scope with no "only" (fork F14)

DECLARE `s 489A party` IS ONE OF
    `s 489A the audit committee`
    `s 489A the directors`

DECLARE `s 489A act` IS ONE OF
    `s 489A(3)(a) make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment`
    `s 489A(3)(b) propose an auditor or auditors for appointment`

-- src:6817 | (3) Before an appointment to which this section applies is made—
-- src:6818 | (a) the audit committee of the company must make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment, and
-- src:6819 | (b) the directors must propose an auditor or auditors for appointment ...
@ref s 489A(3)(a) Before an appointment the audit committee must make a recommendation (src:6817-6819)
GIVEN `the number of days before the appointment is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 489A party` `s 489A act`
`s 489A(3)(a) the audit committee must make a recommendation to the directors before the appointment is made` MEANS
    PARTY `s 489A the audit committee`
    MUST `s 489A(3)(a) make a recommendation to the directors in connection with the appointment`
    WITHIN `the number of days before the appointment is made`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 489A the audit committee` BECAUSE "s 489A(3)(a): the audit committee did not make a recommendation to the directors before the appointment was made"

-- src:6817 | (3) Before an appointment to which this section applies is made—
