        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they cease to hold office at the conclusion of the accounts meeting next following their appointment": that meeting has not concluded (a period the text fixes in its own words: ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:6877 | (2) This is without prejudice to the provisions of this Part as to removal and resignation of auditors.
@ref s 491(2) Without prejudice to the provisions of this Part as to removal and resignation of auditors (src:6877-6877)
GIVEN `the provision is one of the provisions of Part 16 as to removal and resignation of auditors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491(2) the term of office rule prejudices the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is one of the provisions of Part 16 as to removal and resignation of auditors`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is without prejudice to the provisions of this Part as to removal and resignation of auditors"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving names only the provisions on removal and resignation
